{"transcript":"distinguished son of the Ningo-Prampram constituency our father colleague and comrade Honorable bb kabo affectionately known as BB his passing reminds us of life's inevitable reality and the sovereignty of God who in his infinite wisdom has called him home Honorable bibi kabu lived a life marked by dedication service and commitment to the welfare of his people and the development of his community and the constituency he was among the founding members of the Eagle Club established between nineteen ninety one and nineteen ninety two within the Ningo-Prampram traditional area this group later evolved into the National Democratic Congress NDC when the party was formally launched in June nineteen ninety two in his quest to strengthen the party and promote democratic governance Honorable kabu served as the first chairman of the Greater Accra regional executive committee of the NDC the party took root in his personal office before we officially got a space of our own his dedication to the party's ideals and his commitment to grassroot mobilization significantly contributed to the party's growth and consolidation in the Ningo-Prampram constituency and in the Greater Accra region in the landmark nineteen ninety two parliamentary elections Honorable bb kabu contested the parliamentary seat for the Ningo-Prampram constituency alongside other notable candidates from the constituency with confidence and widespread public support he emerged victorious he was duly elected as the first member of parliament for the ninggu Prampram constituency in the fourth republic of Ghana during his tenure as member of parliament Honorable kabu showed exceptional leadership and commitment to developing the constituency notably he oversaw the construction of the road from Dwena through Prampram and New Ningo to Djange Bridge which significantly improved transportation and directly enabled increased socioeconomic activities within the constituency Mister Speaker additionally during his tenure as member of parliament he initiated the idea of bridging the Densu lagoon between New Ningo and Old Ningo this followed a visit by the president flight lieutenant JJ Rawlings to both communities the initiative reflected his vision of improving connectivity and fostering development across the constituency mister speaker within his four year term in parliament honorable BB Kabu facilitated several developmental projects that continue to benefit the people of Ningo-Prampram among these was the construction of head teachers bungalows in several district assembly schools including those in New Ningo Dawena and other communities within the constituency he also championed the upgrading of numerous township roads particularly in New Ningo and surrounding communities honorable speaker mister Kabu belonged to a class of his own in style and poise when he spoke you heard the voice of a sage and the words of the ancestors his fashion sense was impeccable few could match his looks in any room BB entered in this chamber today only mister speaker the honorable right Alban Sumana Kingsford Bagbin and the honorable Collins Dauda served alongside him from the first parliament of the fourth republic mister speaker beyond his achievements in public service honorable Kabu was admired by his humility integrity and strong commitment his leadership extended beyond politics to the strengthening of families traditional institutions and party structures he we cannot overlook the leadership and guidance he gave not only to his Kabu Ope Toto family but also to the Ningo-Prampram constituency the Katamanso NDC party and the nation his legacy of dedication honesty and service will stay with us mister speaker on behalf of the constituency executives council of elders the entire membership of the Ningo-Prampram constituency of the National Democratic Congress both past and present and on behalf of myself as the mp honorable sam nate George on whose behalf I read this we extend our deepe